w fast can a prefab house be completed in Nepal?","answer":"A typical 2-story residential prefab home can be manufactured in 5–7 days and assembled on site within 10–15 days, saving over 60% construction time compared to brick and mortar."},{"id":"fq5","question":"What is the difference between EPS and PUF sandwich panels?","answer":"EPS (Expanded Polystyrene) panels are lightweight, cost-effective, and ideal for residential homes and partition walls. PUF (Polyurethane Foam) panels offer higher R-value thermal density, making them optimal for cold storage and extreme temperature control."},{"id":"fq6","question":"Can Smart Prefab Panel buildings be used in hilly and mountain regions of Nepal?","answer":"Absolutely. Our lightweight prefab system is ideal for remote hill districts where transporting heavy materials is difficult. Panels can be transported by smaller vehicles and assembled without heavy machinery."},{"id":"fq7","question":"Do you provide installation services across all 77 districts?","answer":"Yes. We have an authorised dealer and installation network across all 77 districts of Nepal, ensuring professional assembly and after-sales support regardless of your project location."},{"id":"fq8","question":"What thickness of EPS panel should I choose for my home?","answer":"For standard residential walls in Nepal's climate, 75mm EPS is most popular, offering a good balance of insulation and strength. 50mm is used for interior partitions and 100mm for cold storage or extreme weather applications."},{"id":"fq9","question":"Is a dealership available in my district?","answer":"We are rapidly expanding our dealer network. Visit our Dealership page to apply or contact our sales team to check availability in your area. We provide training, marketing support and factory direct pricing to all authorised dealers."},{"id":"fq10","question":"Do Smart Prefab Panel products meet Nepal National Building Code?","answer":"Yes. All our structural systems are designed by licensed civil and structural engineers to comply with the Nepal National Building Code (NBC), including seismic zone requirements for the Kathmandu Valley and other earthquake-prone areas."}]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"py-10 md:py-16 lg:py-20 bg-brand-cream/60 border-t border-gray-100","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-page grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-7","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-orange font-bold","children":"Latest Disclosure"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-blue-dark mt-1 mb-5 sm:mb-7","children":"Official Notices"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3 sm:space-y-4","children":[["$","div","1",{"className":"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display font-bold text-brand-blue-dark text-sm sm:text-base","children":"Notice of 5th Annual General Meeting"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-1","children":"Notice is hereby given to all shareholders regarding the 5th Annual General Meeting to be held at the company's head office, Tinkune 32, Subidanagar, Kathmandu."}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-semibold text-brand-blue bg-brand-cream px-2.5 sm:px-3 py-1 rounded-full shrink-0","children":"2026-08-15"}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display font-bold text-brand-blue-dark text-sm sm:text-base","children":"Dealership Expansion Programme 2026 — Applications Open"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs 